to a date, committing to anything.

00:14:02.609 --> 00:14:08.550
Um, they would regularly ghost girls,
including me, um, right after...

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.660
I'm sorry, what do you call?

00:14:10.875 --> 00:14:11.725
What do you mean ghost?

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:12.405
What does that mean?

00:14:12.465 --> 00:14:13.085
I'm not familiar...

00:14:13.085 --> 00:14:15.375
That's a, that's a modern dating term.

00:14:15.615 --> 00:14:19.575
It basically means when a person just
stops responding to you, like whether

00:14:19.575 --> 00:14:23.325
you were, uh, in contact, oh, via
phone calls or texting or something.

00:14:23.625 --> 00:14:26.005
Um, it might even that you
already agreed to a date.

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.950
And then on that same day,
they just don't show up.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.310
They don't ever reach out again,
and they just completely disappear.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.200
No explanation whatsoever.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:39.330
And I've experienced that with, you know,
friends to a very extreme degree where

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:42.660
they literally were so over the top.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:46.680
At first it's called love bombing
in the dating, uh, language.

00:14:47.099 --> 00:14:50.459
Um, where they would, like my one
friend for example, was scheduled to

00:14:50.459 --> 00:14:54.660
meet this guy's parents and 'cause
he was so all over her and then

00:14:54.689 --> 00:14:59.640
