and if I personally, that's my theory,

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:33.470
I feel like this has to do with
the American fear of confrontation.

00:16:33.475 --> 00:16:38.760
A lot of Americans just do not like
telling the other person that...

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:42.400
anything negative really, that they're
not interested or that they did a bad job.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:45.210
There's just such a big fear of
confrontation that for a lot of

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:48.610
these people, I think this ghosting
method is the easiest for them.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.980
It's the most comfortable for them.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:52.800
In Germany, I would argue
that doesn't really exist.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.075
So most of my friends in their twenties
are in long-term relationships,

00:16:57.075 --> 00:16:58.545
maybe even live with their partner.

00:16:58.785 --> 00:16:59.055
It's...

00:16:59.265 --> 00:17:02.475
germany is not as, you know, religious
and conservative in that sense.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.025
It doesn't, just because you move
